(=== UNIT 3: IDEATION & CREATIVE PROBLEM SOLVING ===) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 3.1 Divergent vs. Convergent Thinking Dynamics) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Creative engineering problem solving requires deliberate rhythmic alternation between) Tj
T*
(two contrasting cognitive phases:) Tj
T*
(* Divergent Thinking: The cognitive process of exploring an expansive space of) Tj
T*
(diverse, wild, and non-obvious ideas without premature evaluation. Prioritizes) Tj
T*
(quantity over quality: 'To have a good idea, you must first have many ideas' \(Linus) Tj
T*
(Pauling\).) Tj
T*
(* Convergent Thinking: The analytical process of clustering, filtering, evaluating,) Tj
T*
(and selecting the most promising concepts based on objective feasibility,) Tj
T*
(desirability, and viability criteria.) Tj
T*
(* The Golden Rule of Ideation: Strictly separate Divergent Generation from Convergent) Tj
T*
(Evaluation. Simultaneous judgment kills creative risk-taking.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 3.2 Brainstorming Rules and Techniques) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* The 7 Cardinal Rules of Brainstorming \(IDEO / Stanford d.school\):) Tj
T*
(- 1. Defer judgment \(no criticism, snickering, or immediate dismissals\).) Tj
T*
(- 2. Encourage wild and crazy ideas \(breakthroughs emerge from extreme thinking\).) Tj
T*
(- 3. Build on the ideas of others \('Yes, and...' rather than 'No, but...'\).) Tj
T*
(- 4. Stay focused on the topic \(anchor to the HMW prompt\).) Tj
T*
(- 5. One conversation at a time \(preserve shared cognitive bandwidth\).) Tj
T*
(- 6. Be visual \(sketching, sticky notes, visual diagrams\).) Tj
T*
(- 7. Go for quantity \(aim for 100+ ideas in a 45-minute sprint\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 3.3 Structured Ideation Frameworks: SCAMPER and Reverse Thinking) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* SCAMPER Technique \(Alex Osborn / Bob Eberle\):) Tj
T*
(- Substitute: What components, materials, or steps can be swapped?) Tj
T*
(- Combine: What features, modules, or services can be fused together?) Tj
T*
(- Adapt: How can an existing solution from another industry be repurposed?) Tj
T*
(- Modify / Magnify / Minify: What can be enlarged, scaled down, or exaggerated?) Tj
T*
(- Put to another use: Can the product serve a completely new customer segment?) Tj
T*
(- Eliminate: What complex features or steps can be ruthlessly removed?) Tj
T*
(- Reverse / Rearrange: What happens if the workflow sequence is inverted?) Tj
T*
(* Reverse Thinking \(Inversion / Worst Possible Idea\): Instead of asking how to solve) Tj
T*
