T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: Overcoming dominating team personalities in rural water purification) Tj
T*
(ideation using the structured Brainwriting 6-3-5 protocol.) Tj
T*
(Methodology Execution:) Tj
T*
(6 participants, 3 ideas each, written on sheets of paper passed every 5 minutes for 6) Tj
T*
(rounds \(yielding 6 x 3 x 6 = 108 distinct ideas in 30 minutes\).) Tj
T*
(Evolution of an Idea across Rounds:) Tj
T*
(Round 1: Use ceramic clay filters to remove turbidity.) Tj
T*
(Round 2 \(Build\): Impregnate clay with colloidal silver nanoparticles to kill bacteria) Tj
T*
(without boiling.) Tj
T*
(Round 3 \(Build\): Add activated carbon from local coconut husks to adsorb pesticide) Tj
T*
(runoff and unpleasant odors.) Tj
T*
(Round 4 \(Build\): Design a gravity-fed drip assembly using standard discarded paint) Tj
T*
(buckets to eliminate pumps.) Tj
T*
(Round 5 \(Build\): Partner with local pottery cooperatives for sustainable village) Tj
T*
(manufacturing and maintenance.) Tj
T*
(Outcome: A low-cost $8.00 community water purifier manufactured entirely from locally) Tj
T*
(sourced clay, silver, and coconut charcoal.) Tj
T*
