/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 3.5 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Differentiate between Divergent and Convergent thinking, explaining why) Tj
T*
(separating them is essential for creative problem solving.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Divergent thinking is the generative cognitive mode where individuals explore an) Tj
T*
(expansive problem space, making unconventional conceptual associations and producing a) Tj
T*
(massive quantity of wild, diverse ideas without immediate judgment. Convergent thinking) Tj
T*
(is the analytical mode where ideas are organized, screened against technical) Tj
T*
(constraints, prioritized, and synthesized into viable solutions. Conflating both modes) Tj
T*
(simultaneously causes 'premature convergence': critical analysis kills nascent creative) Tj
T*
(concepts before they can be refined. Successful design teams deliberately alternate) Tj
T*
(between dedicated divergent brainstorming sprints and rigorous convergent screening) Tj
T*
(sessions.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain the SCAMPER ideation framework and demonstrate its application to an) Tj
T*
(engineering product or process.) Tj
T*
(Answer: SCAMPER is a creative thinking checklist consisting of seven stimulus triggers:) Tj
T*
(Substitute \(replace materials or steps\), Combine \(integrate complementary features\),) Tj
T*
(Adapt \(borrow solutions from other domains\), Modify/Magnify/Minify \(scale up or down\),) Tj
T*
(Put to other use \(target new markets\), Eliminate \(remove unnecessary complexity\), and) Tj
T*
(Reverse/Rearrange \(invert sequences\). In civil engineering, precast modular construction) Tj
T*
(exemplifies SCAMPER: Substitute \(factory concrete for site-cast concrete\), Combine) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
